# Shorter I2C controller reset on the DAC's bus (gapless transition cost).
name: i2c-reset-pulse
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03060338
gate: build refuses unless the 6 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: The DAC register writer (0x03060c4c) brings the I2C controller
  up for every write and takes it down after (0x0306021c init, transfer,
  0x0306043a deinit). For buses 0-2 the init holds the controller's CRU
  soft reset 0x1a for delay_ms(1) (0x03060338). A track start writes
  seven DAC registers (mute, rate, volume, unmute) before the I2S DMA
  restarts, so that hold alone is 7 ms of every track-change gap
  (measured in patches/gapless/rig/). A soft-reset hold needs a few
  cycles of the block's clock, which 0x0306032c ungates just before.
  This patch holds it for delay_us(50) instead: `movs r0, #50` and the
  BL retargeted from delay_ms 0x03064944 to delay_us 0x03064920.
  Buses 3-8 keep the stock 1 ms hold. Bytes:
  patches/gapless/tools/assemble_v2.py.
expect: 012004f003fb
replace: 322004f0f1fa
